course: dictionary
lesson: 5044
title: Inlets and openings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An inlet is a narrow piece of sea or lake water that reaches into the land, like a small bay. The word "in" in inlet is a clue: the water goes in.
explain: «Ice is thinner near moving water, such as streams, inlets and under bridges.» The sentence lists inlets with streams and places under bridges, so they must be water places, not land. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and check that it still makes sense.
explain: The word has a second meaning, used for machines and pipes. An inlet is an opening that lets water, air or fuel go in. An outlet is the opposite: it lets things out. Each sense is clear once you read the words around it.
fact: An inlet is a narrow area of sea or lake water that goes into the land.
fact: An inlet can also be an opening through which water, air or fuel goes into a machine or pipe.
fact: An inlet pipe lets something in, and an outlet lets it out.
fact: In geography, an inlet is a coastal feature, like a bay, cove or fjord.
fact: «Ice is thinner near moving water, such as streams, inlets and under bridges.» This is why ice near inlets can be unsafe.
exercise: «Ice is thinner near moving water, such as streams, inlets and under bridges.» What is an inlet in this sentence? | *A narrow area of water going into the land | A machine that makes ice | A kind of bridge | A high cliff above the sea
exercise: A tank fills with water through its inlet pipe. What does an inlet do? | It lets something out | It makes the water cold | It stops the water from moving | *It lets something in
exercise: For a pipe, which word is the opposite of inlet? | Bridge | *Outlet | Cove | Stream
test: The boat sailed into the narrow inlet, away from the big waves. Where did the boat go? | A deep hole dug in the ground | A machine for pumping air | *A small bay of water reaching into the land | A high wall built on the coast
test: Water flows into the tank through its ___ pipe. Which word fills the gap? | glacier | bridge | outlet | *inlet
exam: Which word fits best: an ___ is a narrow arm of sea that reaches into the land? | stream | *inlet | glacier | outlet
